  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for South Sudanese Refugees and Host Communities in Uganda</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">Unterst&#xfc;tzung s&#xfc;dsudanesischer Fl&#xfc;chtlinge und aufnehmender Gemeinden in Uganda (VP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">Mit dem Vorhaben soll ein Beitrag zur Sicherung der Lebensgrundlagen sowie zur Verbesserung der sozio&#xf6;konomischen Entwicklungsm&#xf6;glichkeiten f&#xfc;r Fl&#xfc;chtlinge und Bewohner aufnehmender Gemeinden in Uganda geleistet werden. Gleichzeitig soll die friedliche Koexistenz zwischen den Bev&#xf6;lkerungsgruppen gef&#xf6;rdert werden. Ziel des Moduls ist, dass der Refugee Response Fund (RRF) beim Projekttr&#xe4;ger Office of the Prime Minister etabliert ist und &#xfc;ber Implementierungspartner bedarfsorientiert Infrastrukturvorhaben finanziert. In zwei Fast-Track-Projekten sollen (1) Ma&#xdf;nahmen im WASH-Bereich in dem Siedlungsgebiet Rhino Camp durch die NRO Oxfam und (2) Ma&#xdf;nahmen im Bildungsbereich in dem Siedlungsgebiet Bidibidi durch die NRO Save the Children durchgef&#xfc;hrt werden. Die Gesamtkosten der ersten Phase des Programms belaufen sich auf 10 Mio. EUR.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Programme concerns the support of the intensive efforts of the Ugandan government to address the needs of the refugees and host communities. For this purpose, a Refugee Response Fund (RRF) is set up to allow for a transparent and efficient selection, financing and monitoring process for projects in the refugee context. The Office of the Prime Minister is responsible for the implementation of the RRF. Under the RRF, two fast-track projects are implemented targeting both refugees and host communities: 1.The first project shall improve the drinking water and sanitation situation in Rhino camp, implemented by Oxfam.2.The second project shall improve the education situation in Bidibidi Settlement, implemented by Save the Children (Oxfam and Save the Children together hereinafter referred to as the NGOs). The purpose of the Programme is that the RRF finances and monitors the fast-track projects and that the created infrastructure is utilized by the population/target group. This is to contribute to securing basic needs as well as to the social and economic development of refugees and people in host communities.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Programme concerns the support of the intensive efforts of the Ugandan government to address the needs of the refugees and host communities. For this purpose, a Refugee Response Fund (RRF) is set up to allow for a transparent and efficient selection, financing and monitoring process for projects in the refugee context. The Office of the Prime Minister is responsible for the implementation of the RRF. Under the RRF, two fast-track projects are implemented targeting both refugees and host communities: 1.The first project shall improve the drinking water and sanitation situation in Rhino camp, implemented by Oxfam.2.The second project shall improve the education situation in Bidibidi Settlement, implemented by Save the Children (Oxfam and Save the Children together hereinafter referred to as the NGOs). The purpose of the Programme is that the RRF finances and monitors the fast-track projects and that the created infrastructure is utilized by the population/target group. This is to contribute to securing basic needs as well as to the social and economic development of refugees and people in host communities.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">&#xdc;bergeordnetes entwicklungspolitisches Ziel ist es, einen Beitrag zur Sicherung der Lebensgrundlagen sowie zur Verbesserung der sozio&#xf6;konomischen Entwicklung der Fl&#xfc;chtlinge und der Bewohner aufnehmender Gemeinden in Norduganda zu leisten.</narrative>
  </description>
